       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Your confirming it doesn't resolve either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose for adults. Your confirmation doesn't change the patient's risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, or cardiovascular harm.\n- **The confirmation needs to come from a prescriber.** A finance analyst can't verify that this dose is clinically intended, so it doesn't count as clinician sign-off.\n\n**Options:**\n- The prescribing clinician can contact me directly and confirm the dose. If they have a clinical reason for exceeding the maximum, they should enter or co-sign the order themselves and involve pharmacy.\n- If the intended regimen is within the usual range, I can enter it once a clinician confirms it. Examples are ibuprofen 400 mg or 600 mg orally every 6 hours (4 times daily), or 800 mg orally every 8 hours (3 times daily).\n\nIf this order was meant for a real patient, please contact the treating team or pharmacy now so the patient gets appropriate care."
